From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:32:13 +0900
Subject: Android host: the phone turns as Android turns it,
 also from display settings

A quarter turn of the phone output in display settings (kcm_kscreen), or a mode across its
current orientation (2400x1080 while upright), used to rotate KWin's picture into the host's
upright buffers (a third of the screen drawn, the rest black) and was saved, so it came back
with the next session. Now it asks Android to turn the phone (the platform bridge's
"orientation", as the Android device panel does); the host then offers the turned size, which
the output takes as any host resize. The phone output never takes a transform of its own,
neither a user's nor a saved one replayed at start. A turn is relative: the settings show the
turned phone upright again, so a quarter turn goes from upright to landscape and back.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
